<title>SPAIN: Accord seen in Spain labour talks - employers head.</title>
<headline>Accord seen in Spain labour talks - employers head.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jose Maria Cuevas, the president of Spain's employers association CEOE, said on Thursday he expected unions and employers to reach an accord on labour reform without government intervention.</p>
<p>&quot;I expect that within the next days we can announce that we have arrived at an important level of approximation that will allow us to say that we have reached an agreement,&quot; Cuevas said.</p>
<p>Talks between the two have been tough and the government has warned it would step in next month if an acceptable agreement is not reached.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
